  "description": "Team,\n\nBelow is a consolidated overview of our current contributors, release milestones, partner companies, and source repositories.\u202fJohn\u202fDoe (Launchpad\u202fID\u202fjohn.doe, Gerrit\u202fID\u202fjdoe) is reachable at john.doe@example.com and was with Acme\u202fCorp until\u202f2022\u2011Jun\u201130.\u202fAlice\u202fSmith (Launchpad\u202fID\u202falice.smith) can be contacted via alice.smith@openstack.org or a.smith@acme.com.  \n\nWe are tracking two major releases: **v1.0**, which is slated to close on\u202f2023\u2011Mar\u201115, and **v2.0**, scheduled for\u202f2024\u2011Jul\u201130. Our corporate partners include **Acme\u202fCorp** (domains\u202facme.com,\u202facme.org) and the **OpenStack\u202fFoundation** (domain\u202fopenstack.org).  \n\nFor code assets, the OpenStack\u202fNova project lives at https://github.com/openstack/nova. It is a Git repository under the OpenStack organization, classified in the Compute project group, and the module name is \u201cnova\u201d. The repository maintains the\u202fmaster\u202fand\u202fstable/2023.1\u202fbranches, and the v1.0 release maps tags\u202fv1.0.0\u202fthrough\u202fv1.0.9. The Acme web application is hosted at https://gitlab.com/acme/webapp, also a Git repository belonging to the Acme organization with the module name \u201cwebapp\u201d, and currently only the\u202fmain\u202fbranch is active."
